      "description": "Watch Al Ittihad FC vs Al Kholood highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. On August 15, 2026 , the Pro League played host to a captivating encounter between Al Ittihad FC and Al Kholood . Both teams stepped onto the pitch with high ambitions, setting the stage for a match filled with tactical battles and significant individual moments. First Half Drama and Clinical Finishing The opening exchanges were characterized by physical play, leading to an early yellow card for Coba da Costa in the 21st minute. The atmosphere reached a fever pitch in the 32nd minute when Al Ittihad FC were awarded a penalty. However, the stadium fell silent as Houssem Aouar failed to convert from the spot, missing a golden opportunity to take the lead. That miss proved costly just before the break. In the 43rd minute, Ahmed Al-Julaydan turned provider, setting up Youssef En-Nesyri , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. After six minutes of stoppage time, the first half concluded with the momentum firmly shifted by that late breakthrough. Second Half Surges and a Red Card Twist The second period began with renewed energy, and it wasn't long before the scoreboard moved again. In the 52nd minute, Shaquille Pinas delivered a precise pass to Julien Domingues , who finished clinically to extend the lead. However, the complexion of the game changed entirely in the 58th minute when Danilo Pereira was shown a straight red card. The decision sparked heavy protests from his teammates, leaving his side to navigate the final half-hour with ten men. As the match progressed, the intensity remained high, and Muhannad Shanqeeti was cautioned in the 66th minute. A flurry of substitutions followed, with managers looking to manage the closing stages. Players like Moussa Diaby , Youssef En-Nesyri , and eventually Houssem Aouar made way for fresh legs. Despite nine minutes of added time at the end of the match, the initial drama of the second half proved to be the defining factor in this hard-fought contest."
